AB  - The proceedings contain 184 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining. The topics include: From Moderation to Mediation: Can LLMs Serve as Mediators in Online Flame Wars?; a Regime-Aware Fusion Framework for Time Series Classification; on Imbalanced Regression with Hoeffding Trees; Multi-RAG: A Multimodal Retrieval-Augmented Generation System for Adaptive Video Understanding; hybrid Time Series Diffusion Model and Conformal Prediction for Incomplete Time Series; nCLEAR: Nonlinear Coupled Latent Embedding for Cross-Sectional Asset Returns; Facet-Level Persona Control by Trait-Activated Routing with Contrastive SAE for Role-Playing LLMs; AI-Generated Image Detection Based on the Most Suspicious Patch; GROFF: A Generative Restoration Model for Occluded Face Filling; q-Matrix Completeness and Annotation Strategies: A Comparative Study of Knowledge Tracing Architectures; HSGTCN: A Hybrid Semantic-Guided Transformer-CNN Network for Learned Image Compressed Sensing; STEPS: Scene Text Editing with Preserved Style Using Diffusion and Contrastive Style Encoding; Semantic-Enhanced Representation Architecture for Automatic ICD Coding via Hyperbolic Graph Neural Networks; approximately Bisubmodular Regret Minimization in Billboard and Social Media Advertising; what Helps—and What Hurts: Bidirectional Explanations for Vision Transformers; Adaptive PII Detection via Evolutionary Orchestration and Multi-agent Debate; cloud–Edge Collaborative Anomaly Detection for Water Treatment Systems; CONAN: CONcept-Oriented ANomaly Detector for Interpretable Zero-Shot Detection; Automated Multiple-Choice Question Generation: A Survey from a KDDM Perspective; Graph Neural Networks in EEG-Based Emotion Recognition: A Survey; generative Artificial Intelligence for Project Management: A Review of Architectures, Applications, and Governance; A Review of Human-Centric Evaluation of Cultural Biases in Indic Languages in LLMs: Rethinking Research Direc