TI  - Enhancing Sentiment Classification Accuracy in Myanmar YouTube Comments Using a Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM Attention Model
AU  - Reddy, Y.T.
AU  - Suvarchala, K.
AU  - Goud, N.S.C.
AU  - Sarda, V.
T2  - 2026 2nd International Conference on Big Data and Machine Learning, ICBDML 2026
AB  - Comments posted on YouTube have become a valuable source of opinion mining with the swift growth of user-generated content on social media. Even though SA has already made impressive feats with the English language, computational implementation of sentiment analysis tasks with low-resource languages, including Myanmar, is still difficult, as it has a complicated agglutinative morphology and no whitespace-delimiting characters. This study suggests a strong model of classifying sentiment polarities of Myanmar posts on YouTube in terms of positive and negative polarities. Our hypothesis is that a new architecture, the Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM with Attention Mechanism (HCB-AM), will be able to surmount the distinctive peculiarities of the Myanmar script.It employs CNNs to obtain local features on n-grams and BiLSTM networks to obtain the context of long texts. It has an attention mechanism, which its aim is to concentrate on important words and not noisy words. The paper performs research on a manually annotated dataset of 9,902 comments on viral Myanmar music videos. We have done extensive preprocessing, such as syllable-based segmentation and removal of stop-words to clean up the noisy text. We made comparisons on the proposed architecture and the standard deep learning models, which are RNN, GRU, and simple LSTM. It has been demonstrated through experiment that deep learning can be highly effective in the field, and the LSTM baseline reporting an accuracy of 97%. The suggested hybrid model increases the performance even further and provides a scaling method of sentiment analysis in under-resourced languages.  © 2026 IEEE.
