TY  - CONF
TI  - FinHybridSA: A sentiment detection model for financial social media text used for financial decision-making
AU  - Yu, Z.
T2  - Proceedings of 2026 International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Fintech, IC-AIF 2026
AB  - Sentiment analysis in financial texts remains challenging due to the prevalence of domain-specific language patterns on social media. To address these challenges, this paper proposes a hybrid semantic-symbolic framework, FinHybridSA, which combines contextual embeddings with interpretable domain features. The system consists of two modules: an intensity recognition module and an uncertainty detection module. These features are fused with the semantic representations of a large language model (BERT) and fed into a multilayer perceptron classifier. Experimental results show that FinHybridSA maintains superior performance with limited training data compared to benchmark models, while also exhibiting higher interpretability and robustness. Ablation experiments confirm that symbolic features can capture subtle emotional phenomena in financial social texts, thereby continuously improving classification accuracy. Our research demonstrates the effectiveness of hybrid representation learning as a resource-efficient alternative for sentiment analysis in financial texts.  © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
