TY  - CONF
TI  - Emotion Detection in Gujarati Text: Evaluation of Machine Learning Classifiers with Bag-of-Words and TF-IDF Feature Extraction Techniques
AU  - Patil, K.
AU  - Nasriwala, J.
AU  - Savant, R.
AU  - Bhatt, P.
T2  - Communications in Computer and Information Science
A2  - Tiwari S.
A2  - Ortiz-Rodríguez F.
A2  - Shivakumar A.
A2  - Shimizu C.
AB  - In the model digital era, social media platforms have become central hub for an individual to express their thoughts, opinion and emotions in various form of textual data. Text classification tasks such as sentiment analysis, and emotion detection from the text is increasing day-by-day for the applications such as social media analysis, customer feedback and interpretation and mental health monitoring. This study presents an emotion detection from Gujarati text which is a low resource and morphologically rich Indian Language. It also employs four machine learning classifiers namely Naïve Bayes, Logistic Regression, Support Vector Machine (SVM), and Random Forest along with two feature extraction technique BoW and TF_IDF. The performance of the model is evaluated using confusion matrix which provides class wise as well as overall accuracy. The outcome reveals that Random Forest achieves highest accuracy followed by SVM classifier. Overall, using this approach the accuracy of the emotion detection from Gujarati text is increased. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.
