TI  - CVT-FoMO: A Framework for the Association between Creator Induction Strategies and Collective FoMO in Cryptocurrency Video Subtitles
AU  - Chen, K.
AU  - Jia, K.
T2  - Proceedings of 2026 International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Fintech, IC-AIF 2026
AB  - To address the scarcity of fine-grained, dual-source data in cryptocurrency FoMO research, we introduce CVT-FoMO, a bilingual dataset of 16,187 transcript-comment pairs. We further propose an optimized prompting strategy integrating Role-Playing (RP), Few-Shot (FS), and Chain-of-Thought (CoT). Experimentsdemonstrate that this strategy achieves an 85% human win rate, significantly outperforming baselines. Further analysis reveals distinct asset-specific FoMO drivers (e.g., value anxiety for Bitcoin vs. meme-narratives for Dogecoin) and validates an "Induction-Resonance"mechanism, where creator agendas are statistically amplified by audience interactions (k = 0.28). This study provides a robust benchmark for sentiment analysis and platform risk governance.  © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
