AB  - The proceedings contain 580 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Pattern Recognition and Computer Vision,. The topics include: TMFit: Enhancing Fashion Image Editing Precision via Text-Driven Mask Generation; dreamDancer: Music-Driven Dance Video Intelligent Generation; VSE-MQA: A Semantic Grouping and Multi-modal Approach for Accurate Video Quality Assessment; enhancing Compositional Reasoning in Multimodal Large Language Models; latentEdit: Adaptive Latent Control for Consistent Semantic Editing; clinCoCoOp: An Interpretable Prompt Learning Framework with Clinical Concept Guidance for Context Optimization; all-in-Focus Seeing Through Occlusions with Event and Frame; capturing Cross-Modal Semantics by Generating Comments for Image-Text Contents; false Negatives Do Matter: A Novel Soft Label and Reranking Based Plug-in Method for Image-Text Retrieval; uncertainty-Aware Deep Anchor Graph Learning for Multimodal Remote Sensing Image Clustering; CFANet: Cross-Frequency Adaptive Fusion with Frequency-Modulated Attention for Multi-focus Image Fusion; adaptive Multimodal Fusion for Graph Learning in Brain Disease Prediction; SentiMM: A Multimodal Multi-agent Framework for Sentiment Analysis in Social Media; Bias-Unlearning in MABSA: A Causal Framework with Cross-Modal Counterfactual Inference; mapping Semantic, Unmasking Falsehoods: Topic-Driven Hierarchical Graph Network for Short Video Fake News Detection; revisiting Symmetric Teacher-Student Network Distillation for Anomaly Detection; user-Adjustable Image Cropping Based on Visual Semantic Awareness; multi-source Domain Adaptation Image Steganalysis for Cover Source Mismatch; PhoneGuide-SLAM: Low-Cost Smartphone Navigation for the Visually Impaired Using Visual Semantic SLAM; fairMoE: Decoupled Expert Learning for Unbiased Customized Face Generation; strategyAdapter: One-Shot Learning for Unseen-Domain Procedural Sequence Generation; divide, Weight, and Route: Difficulty-Aware Optimization with Dynamic Expert Fusion for Long-Tailed Recognition; c3F: A Coarse-to-Fine Feature Fusion Approach for Scene Script Identification; secure and Scalable Face Retrieval via Cancelable Product Quantization; few-Shot Font Generation via Attribute-Guided Diffusion with Style Contrastive Learning; rethinking the Evaluation of Scene Graph Generation; probabilistic Visual Prompt Tuning.
