AB  - The proceedings contain 29 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Human-Computer Interaction. The topics include: Multimodal Speed Dating Dataset: Behavioral Cues, Psychological Ratings, and Empirical Findings; cross-Cultural Interaction on Social Media Health Platforms: Challenges and Opportunities from Africa; Exploring HIV Conversations: Social Media Interactions and Social Institutions in the LGBTQIA+ Community in the Philippines; content Themes and Self-presentation of Virtual Influencers - Exploring the Impact on User Engagement and Sentiment; analysis of Combined Impact of Information and Emotional Content on User Engagement Based on Social Media Data; Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Secure Environments: Theoretical Foundations, Agent Architectures, and Local Deployment with FAIRD; An Investigation into the Use of LLM-Based Features for Multimodal Estimation of Elderly Engagement in Active Listening; SNS Search System that Uses a Large Language Model to Display Posts on an Interactive Map from Various Perspectives; ChatGPT Usability. An Exploratory Study in Higher Education; Assessing AI-Based System Acceptance Through the Design of a Trustworthiness Estimation Tool for Machine Learning Models; A Comparison of the Coverage of Chat GPT in China Daily and The New York Times Based on Frame Theory and Content Analysis; representating Negative State of a Robot’s Abdominal/Thoracic Breathing Accompanied Movement System; towards a Formal Methodology for Evaluating Information Consumer Experience at Work; unlocking Multilingualism: Thoughts Shaped by Tools?; Estimating Subjective Evaluation on Drinking Experiences Using fNIRS Sensing; internet of Things (IoT) for Weather Monitoring Systems in Rural Zones: Literature Review; key Factors in Patient Satisfaction: A Random Forest Strategy; method for Evaluating Cyber Risk Management Frameworks; evaluating the Impact of Insider Threats.
