TI  - Cross Domain Sentiment Analysis in Indonesian Using a Transformer-Based Language Model
AU  - Akbar, M.N.
AU  - Wicaksono, A.F.
AU  - Budi, I.
T2  - 2025 10th International Conference on Informatics and Computing, ICIC 2025
AB  - Cross-domain sentiment analysis (CDSA) remains a challenging task, particularly for low-resource languages like Indonesian, where domain shifts can significantly hinder model performance. While pre-trained language models offer promising capabilities, there is a need to understand the most effective adaptation strategies for the Indonesian context. This study compares a traditional machine learning baseline (ExtraTree) against language-specific (IndoBERT) and multilingual (XLM-R) Transformer models for Indonesian CDSA. Using single and multi-source adaptation strategies across four distinct domains of web reviews and social media text, our experiments demonstrate that Transformer-based models consistently outperform the baseline. However, this higher accuracy comes with a significant computational tradeoff, as the baseline is substantially more efficient in both training and inference time. The results show that for single-source adaptation, IndoBERT achieves the best performance with an average Macro F1-score of 0.6851. In contrast, for multi-source adaptation, XLM-R yields the top result with a macro F1-score of 0.7351.  © 2025 IEEE.
