TY  - CONF
TI  - Contextual Emotion Retrieval in Low-Resource Languages: A Deep Neural Paradigm for Bengali Nostalgia Detection
AU  - Sing, B.
AU  - Rahman, M.R.
T2  - 2025 IEEE International Conference on Quantum Photonics, Artificial Intelligence, and Networking, QPAIN 2025
A2  - Shah M.S.
AB  - Nostalgia is a complex emotion that connects individuals to their cultural and personal pasts, often expressed in digital platforms through comments, posts, and narratives. This study focuses on the automatic detection of nostalgic sentiment in Bengali text, a low-resource language with rich cultural depth but limited computational tools. We introduce a manually annotated dataset of 20,561 Bengali comments from different social media categorized as nostalgic or non-nostalgic. The dataset, initially imbalanced, was augmented to improve class distribution and provide a robust benchmark for machine learning and deep learning models. Our methodology includes a comparative evaluation of classical models such as Logistic Regression, SVM, and Random Forest, as well as deep learning models including CNN, LSTM, BiLSTM, and a fine-tuned BERT-based classifier. Experimental results show that the BERT Nostalgia Classifier achieves the highest accuracy of 87.63 % and an F1-score of 0.81, significantly outperforming other models. The findings confirm that deep contextual embeddings are effective for detecting nuanced emotions like nostalgia in resource-scarce languages. This work contributes a novel dataset and a scalable framework for affective computing in Bengali, with potential applications in sentiment analysis, cultural informatics, and emotionally aware recommender systems. © 2025 IEEE.
