TI  - Exploring BERT-Based Models for Sentiment Analysis in the U.S. Airline Reviews
AU  - Zheng, X.
AU  - Huang, J.
AU  - Sangi, R.
AU  - Ihnaini, B.
T2  - Proceedings - 2025 International Conference on Artificial Intelligence, Human-Computer Interaction and Natural Language Processing, ICAHN 2025
AB  - This study presents a comparative analysis of traditional models (CNN, LSTM) and transformer-based architectures (BERT, DistilBERT, GPT-2, RoBERTa, DeBERTa, and ModernBERT) for sentiment classification on the US Airline Twitter dataset. A systematic experimental framework was adopted, including comprehensive data preprocessing and evaluation using accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score metrics. Experimental results demonstrate that transformer-based models outperform traditional models. Among them, ModernBERT achieves the best performance, obtaining 87.02% accuracy, while maintaining a reasonable inference cost. These findings highlight the effectiveness and practicality of transformer-based models in sentiment analysis and encourage further research on model optimization for low-resource environments and multi-label applications.  © 2025 IEEE.
